#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""rfp -- the tool surface a cheap model drives to find PH government notices worth bidding on.

    rfp build                      merge tenders.db + legacy.db (+ tags.db) -> corpus.db
    rfp sql "select ..."           read-only SQL over corpus.db          <- PRIMARY TOOL
    rfp search "<query>" [filters] profile-weighted ranked hits, token-budgeted
    rfp show <id> [id ...]         full scope text, line items, attached documents
    rfp facets "<query>" [filters] counts by work_type/province/mode/ABC band
    rfp profile                    print the resolved profile
    rfp selfcheck                  assert-based tests, no framework

Design: docs/plans/2026-08-08-ph-rfp-search-design.md   Spike: research/ph-rfp-spike/DECISIONS.md

Three load-bearing properties, each asserted in selfcheck():
  1. `sql` cannot write.  corpus.db is opened file:...?mode=ro AND an authorizer denies ATTACH,
     because mode=ro alone does not stop `attach 'w.db' as w; insert into w...`.
  2. `search` output stays inside a per-hit token budget.  Verbose hits drift the economics back
     toward whole-corpus-in-prompt, which does not fit (1.55M tokens > 1M window).
  3. Every filter is null-tolerant.  The measured hazards -- abc null on 39 rows, location null on
     12.2%, closing null on the zombie rows -- fail by OMISSION, the failure mode no user reports.
"""
